'This sample binds late (CreateObject), so there is deliberately NO reference to
'the KeyNub type library here -- the project opens and runs whether or not the
'server happens to be registered on this machine, and the error you get if it is
'not is the one you would get in production.
'
'To switch to early binding for IntelliSense and compile-time checking:
'  Project > References... > browse to KeyNub.dll > tick "KeyNub License Dongle"
'then change modMain's `Dim dongle As Object` to `Dim dongle As KeyNub.Dongle`.
'
'VB6 may rewrite the stdole2.tlb path above the first time it opens this project.
'That is normal -- the reference is resolved by GUID from the registry, and the
'path is only a hint.
